Package: stockcast
Title: Walk-Forward Evaluation of Daily Equity Return and Volatility Forecasts
Version: 1.0.0
Authors@R:
    person("Satvik", "Praveen", email = "satvikpraveen@usf.edu", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: A reproducible research framework for forecasting daily equity
    log returns and realised variance. Implements a strictly out-of-sample
    rolling-origin (walk-forward) evaluation with periodic refitting, a
    registry of statistical and machine-learning forecasters (random walk,
    historical mean, ARIMA, ETS, STL-ETS, elastic net, random forest,
    ARMA-GARCH, EWMA, HAR-RV), proper scoring rules (RMSE, MAE,
    out-of-sample R-squared, CRPS, Winkler score, QLIKE), formal tests of
    predictive ability (Diebold-Mariano with Harvey-Leybourne-Newbold
    correction, Pesaran-Timmermann directional test), and an economic
    evaluation via a transaction-cost-aware trading backtest.
